-- LINEARITY ---------- errors/linear_used_twice_32.march

The linear value `st4` is used more than once here. [linear_used_twice]
Linear values must be consumed exactly once — they cannot be copied or ignored.

21 |         Relay_A.recv_Fourth(s, st4, fn (_again, st5) -> Relay_A.close(s, st5))))
                                    ^^^

    This is a protocol state, and the first use closed the conversation: no step can follow `close`.
    The conversation so far, in protocol `Relay`:

      … 2 earlier steps
      reply:  C -> A : Bool     done
      third:  A -> B : String   done
      fourth: B -> A : Bool     done   <- `A` tried this again
      (end of conversation)     <- `A` can only close here

    `st4` was already consumed here:

20 |         let _done = Relay_A.close(s, st4)
                                          ^^^
    run `march --explain linear_used_twice`


